    {
      "text": "County parcel data: APN 198-17-023 is 1104 W El Camino Real and APN 198-17-029 is 1124 W El Camino Real; city filings list both APNs for the project.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-001098",
        "SRC-002940"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "City filing 25-0869: condominium map keeps unit count as approved under file 2018-7798 (one commercial condominium, 111 residential condominiums, five single-family lots). San Jose Spotlight reports a plan of about 85 for-sale condos and 25 rentals, with financing given as the reason for the change.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-002940",
        "SRC-002939"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Dahlin Group lists a De Anza Properties project named Grape Avenue in Sunnyvale's El Camino corridor: 111 two- to four-bedroom units over an auto dealership (23,000 sq ft ground floor plus 7,000 sq ft mezzanine) and five four-bedroom detached homes on a 3.6-acre site. The page gives no street address.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-002938"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Original application (file 24-0780): demolish three used auto sales buildings; build a seven-story mixed-use building and five two-story single-family homes; zoning ECR-MU33; CEQA under the El Camino Real Specific Plan EIR.",
      "src": [
        "SRC-001520"
      ]
    }
